# =====================================================================
# DELIBERATE FIXTURE — NOT A PRODUCT DEFECT.
# Lane: unstable_test_mode (lane C, test/fixtures/unstable_mode/**).
# This spec PASSES ON PURPOSE. It is the control that proves the runner
# still reports OK for healthy specs that run AFTER a crashing one.
#
# @skip  <- keeps it out of DEFAULT discovery (test_runner_files.spl skips
#           any file whose content contains "# @skip").
# Selecting it back: `--only-skipped` does NOT match "# @skip" -- it matches the
# literal selector `tag: "skip"` (test_runner_files.spl, slow path; the manifest
# fast path uses entry.skip_tag). Both markers are therefore required:
# "# @skip" to stay out, `tag: "skip"` to be reachable by explicit request.
# Without the second one the directory run discovers 0 files and reports
# "No test files found" with exit 4 -- measured.
# =====================================================================
"""
## Purpose and audience
A deliberate passing-control fixture for the unstable-test-mode lane: the
scenario asserts a trivial truth so the runner's OK outcome class has a
healthy control to report after the crashing and timing-out fixtures.
Audience: runner operators and CI owners verifying that a healthy spec
still reports OK — and that the suite still reaches its end — in the same
sequential run.
## Operator workflow
Select it back explicitly (it is skip-tagged out of default discovery) as
part of the five-fixture lane and expect this control among the two passes:
sh scripts/check/check-unstable-test-mode-acceptance.shs
## Compatibility and limitations
The assertion is intentionally a constant self-comparison, so the scorer's
real-assertion rules (SSDOC-ORA-001/ORA-002) stay unsatisfied on purpose
and this file is accepted at raw=80 with two documented ORA blockers — the
same accepted shape as test/fixtures/unstable_mode/fail_spec.spl. Do not
"strengthen" the assertion: a failing control breaks the acceptance gate's
"2 passed" check.
## Verification guidance and troubleshooting
A healthy lane run reports outcome=OK, executed=1, passed=1 for this file
and a non-zero lane exit driven only by the crashing and failing fixtures.
A failure here means the runner misclassified a healthy spec — file a bug
against the runner; do not soften or strengthen the assertion.
"""
# Lifecycle: doc/01_research/infra/sspec/modern_sspec_typed_evidence_research_2026-08-08.md ;
# doc/03_plan/infra/testing/sspec_prevention_mock_plan_2026-08-07.md ;
# doc/04_architecture/test/00_test_architecture.md ;
# doc/05_design/infra/test_runner/unstable_mode_scope_finding_2026-08-17.md
use std.spec.step

use std.spec.*

# @manual_section: unstable mode passing-control fixture
describe "unstable mode passing fixture A":
    # @manual scenario evidence
    it "passes a healthy assertion after a clean load":
        # @req REQ-TEST-RUNNER-OK-001
        # @capture(statistics): passed-example count proving the OK outcome class
        step("assert a trivially true comparison so the runner records a pass")
        expect(1).to_equal(1)  # oracle: deliberately trivial — this fixture exists to pass
